hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15551","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Abi Khuzamah, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, and Sufyan once said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Tell of a medicine we treat with, and ruqyas we seek ruqyah with, and shields we shield with, do they repel anything of the decree of Allah the Blessed and Exalted? He said: They are of the decree of Allah the Blessed and Exalted."
"15552","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi Muhammad ibn al-Walid, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Abi Khizamah, one of Banu al-Harith, from his father, that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell of a medicine we treat with, and ruqyas we seek ruqyah with, and shields we shield with, do they repel anything of the decree of Allah? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is of the decree of Allah the Blessed and Exalted."
"15553","Harun narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr informed me, from Ibn Shihab, that Ibn Abi Khuzamah, one of Banu al-Harith ibn Sad ibn Hudhaym, narrated to him that his father narrated to him that he said: O Messenger of Allah, tell of a medicine we treat with, and ruqyas we seek ruqyah with, and shields we shield with, do they repel anything of the decree of Allah the Blessed and Exalted? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is of the decree of Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"15554","Husayn ibn Muhammad and Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Abi Khuzamah, from his father, he said: My father, and it is the correct one, thus al-Zubaydi said."
